  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "99a5f09e-64d1-474a-b467-34e5341b3472",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        4464,
        1552
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 864,
        "content": "## Find local businesses with OpenMart and add new prospects to Twenty CRM\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow manually runs a prospect search, validates the search settings, and uses OpenMart to find local businesses matching the configured query and location. It normalizes and deduplicates the discovered businesses, compares them against existing Twenty CRM companies by domain, then creates new company records and review tasks only for net-new prospects. It finishes by summarizing how many prospects were created, already existed, or were processed, with early exits for invalid settings or no usable businesses.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Connect and authorize the OpenMart credential used by the search node.\n- Connect and authorize the Twenty CRM credential, ensuring it has permission to read companies and create companies and tasks.\n- Edit the prospect search configuration to set the target query, city, state, and country.\n- Verify the Twenty field mappings, especially company name, domain, website, and task fields, match your Twenty workspace schema.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the configured search terms and location to target different markets, and modify the deduplication or domain-matching logic if your CRM uses a different uniqueness rule."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "83b54886-5af1-48a5-bf4a-60e1a95eea3b",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        5024,
        1744
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 704,
        "height": 608,
        "content": "## Start and validate search\n\nStarts the manual workflow, defines the prospect search parameters, validates that required settings are present, and stops with an explanatory error when they are invalid."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "d57156af-3a14-4284-83ba-f3224e99e30d",
